Scene Description in RDF Triples (Turtle Format)
```turtle
@prefix : <http://cecs571.csulb.edu/ontology/cornercase#> .
@prefix xsd: <http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#> .

:scene1 a :Scene ;
    :scenarioName "HeavyRainAndFogScenario" ;
    :hasCornerCaseType :cc1 .

:cc1 a :StateAnomaly ;
    :hasWeatherCondition :weather1 ;
    :hasRisk :risk1, :risk2, :risk3, :risk4 ;
    :hasObstacle :obstacle1 .

:weather1 a :RainyCondition ;
    :description "Heavy rain reducing visibility" .

:weather2 a :FoggyCondition ;
    :description "Foggy conditions reducing visibility further" .

:risk1 a :WeatherRisk ;
    :description "Reduced visibility due to heavy rain" ;
    :hasSeverityScore :sev1 .

:risk2 a :RoadConditionRisk ;
    :description "Slippery road conditions due to rain" ;
    :hasSeverityScore :sev2 .

:risk3 a :OcclusionRisk ;
    :description "Occlusion of distant objects due to fog" ;
    :hasSeverityScore :sev3 .

:risk4 a :CollisionRisk ;
    :description "Potential collision risk due to reduced visibility and slippery road" ;
    :hasSeverityScore :sev4 .

:obstacle1 a :RoadObject ;
    :description "Wet road surface and potential puddles" .

:sev1 a :SeverityScore ;
    :severityValue "0.9"^^xsd:float .

:sev2 a :SeverityScore ;
    :severityValue "0.85"^^xsd:float .

:sev3 a :SeverityScore ;
    :severityValue "0.8"^^xsd:float .

:sev4 a :SeverityScore ;
    :severityValue "0.95"^^xsd:float .
```

Identified Risks for each risk class:

Risk 1:
Description: Reduced visibility due to heavy rain
Severity Score: 0.9

Risk 2:
Description: Slippery road conditions due to rain
Severity Score: 0.85

Risk 3:
Description: Occlusion of distant objects due to fog
Severity Score: 0.8

Risk 4:
Description: Potential collision risk due to reduced visibility and slippery road
Severity Score: 0.95

---
The scene is classified as a **StateAnomaly** due to the environmental conditions (heavy rain and fog) that are not directly caused by the behavior of actors but rather by the weather and road conditions. The ontology does not explicitly include a combined weather condition, so the individual weather conditions (`RainyCondition` and `FoggyCondition`) are described separately. The risks identified are primarily related to the weather and road conditions.